##RenderMan RIB-Structure 1.1
##Scene A quad asymmetric about both axes, said in RIB
version 3.03
Format 64 48 1
# one sample at each pixel centre under a one pixel box, which the film gives back exactly:
# this picture pins the hider and the shading, and reference-sampled pins the sampling
PixelSamples 1 1
PixelFilter "box" 1 1
Projection "orthographic"
# the defaults are RI_EPSILON and RI_INFINITY, which leave the orthographic depth scale at
# about 2e-38 and collapse every z onto the near plane
Clipping 1 100
WorldBegin
# the shader that means no shading, named rather than left as the default, so the picture
# shows that the shading language draws an unshaded surface unchanged
Surface "constant"
# asymmetric about both axes, so a flipped picture is a failing one. No Color, so it takes the
# RI default of white, as the scene ReferenceTest builds in code does
Polygon "P" [-0.7 -0.2 5  0.3 -0.2 5  0.3 0.8 5  -0.7 0.8 5]
WorldEnd
